+/*!
+ * \brief Hades: whether a picture that is not reconstructed (an HDR10 or HLG one, or the base layer
+ *        of a Dolby Vision stream that is a picture by itself) is mapped to SDR by the bridge, as a
+ *        reconstructed profile 5 one is, where the output takes no HDR
+ *
+ * Where the tone mapping method of the video is that of a reference display
+ * (VS_TONEMAPMETHOD_BT2390): the BT.2390 curve guided by the stream's HDR10 metadata, the
+ * perceptual gamut mapping into BT.709, HDR reference white at the display's white
+ * (dvbridge_sdr_mapping()). Kodi's own methods stay as they were. Only a picture whose colour the
+ * bridge takes: BT.2020 primaries, the matrix of BT.2020 for non-constant luminance, and HLG, or PQ
+ * with a peak that the metadata gives (the mastering display's white or the content's light level:
+ * without either, the curve would have to guess); not interlaced, not stereoscopic, and never the
+ * base layer of a stream whose base layer is no picture by itself (profile 5, which is
+ * reconstructed instead).
+ * \param sdrOutput the output takes no HDR (SupportsPlainMapping() of the window system)
+ * \param reference the method of the video is that of a reference display
+ * \param baseNoPicture a Dolby Vision stream whose base layer is not known to be a picture by
+ *        itself
+ * \param peakKnown PQ: the HDR10 metadata gives a peak (UsablePeak())
+ */
+constexpr bool PlainMappingEligible(bool sdrOutput,
+                                    bool reference,
+                                    bool baseNoPicture,
+                                    bool pq,
+                                    bool hlg,
+                                    bool bt2020,
+                                    bool ncl,
+                                    bool peakKnown,
+                                    bool interlaced,
+                                    bool stereo)
+{
+  return sdrOutput && reference && !baseNoPicture && bt2020 && ncl && (hlg || (pq && peakKnown)) &&
+         !interlaced && !stereo;
+}
+
+//! Hades: a luminance of the HDR10 metadata that the mapping can take as a peak: (0, 10000] cd/m2
+constexpr bool UsablePeak(double nits)
+{
+  return nits > 0 && nits <= 10000;
+}
